## Scenarios

### checked regex SFFI boundary

#### returns a typed compiled regex for a valid pattern

- Verify: returns a typed compiled regex for a valid pattern
   - Expected: regex.is_valid is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: returns a typed compiled regex for a valid pattern")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
match regex_new_checked(r"\d+"):
    case Ok(regex):
        expect(regex.is_valid).to_equal(true)
        regex_destroy(regex)
    case Err(message):
        fail("valid regex was rejected: {message}")
```

</details>

#### returns an error instead of an invalid Regex value

- Verify: returns an error instead of an invalid Regex value
   - Expected: regex_new_checked(r"[invalid").is_ok() is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 3 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: returns an error instead of an invalid Regex value")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
expect(regex_new_checked(r"[invalid").is_ok()).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

#### preserves match and no-match as successful boolean values

- Verify: preserves match and no-match as successful boolean values


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 13 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: preserves match and no-match as successful boolean values")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
match regex_new_checked(r"\d+"):
    case Ok(regex):
        match regex_is_match_checked(regex, "item 42"):
            case Ok(value): expect(value).to_equal(true)
            case Err(message): fail(message)
        match regex_is_match_checked(regex, "none"):
            case Ok(value): expect(value).to_equal(false)
            case Err(message): fail(message)
        regex_destroy(regex)
    case Err(message):
        fail(message)
```

</details>

#### rejects an invalid handle rather than returning false

- Verify: rejects an invalid handle rather than returning false
   - Expected: regex_is_match_checked(invalid, "anything").is_ok() is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: rejects an invalid handle rather than returning false")
val invalid = Regex(handle: 0, pattern: "", is_valid: false)
expect(regex_is_match_checked(invalid, "anything").is_ok()).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

#### keeps one-shot provider failure distinct from no match

- Verify: keeps one-shot provider failure distinct from no match
   - Expected: regex_is_match_quick_checked(r"\d+", "none").is_ok() is true
   - Expected: regex_is_match_quick_checked(r"[invalid", "none").is_ok() is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: keeps one-shot provider failure distinct from no match")
expect(regex_is_match_quick_checked(r"\d+", "none").is_ok()).to_equal(true)
expect(regex_is_match_quick_checked(r"[invalid", "none").is_ok()).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

